# Wireframe: Login Screen

> v1.0.1 — PATCH: fixed landmark notation in shared conventions; surfaced Main App screen ownership assumption.

## Purpose & Flow Context

Unauthenticated user enters email + password to obtain a session. Serves the "Login Flow" step in the Auth flow. Entry: hydration redirect or manual navigation after logout/session expiry. Exit: main app on success.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `_______` | Text input / editable field |
| `[>▼]` | Dropdown | `⚠` | Alert / error message |
| `[○ ●]` | Radio unselected / selected | `#` | Heading |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `main` (no shared app shell — standalone login) |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm.

**App-shell**: No shared shell — full-bleed centered card. The login screen lives outside the authenticated app shell.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Page bg | Full-viewport background | Dark overlay or gradient |
| Card | Login form container | Centered, max 480px |
| Logo area | App logo / branding | Top of card |
| Form body | Email + Password inputs + ErrorBanner + Submit button | Stacked vertically |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. App logo — brand recognition
2. Email input — primary action field
3. Password input — secondary field
4. "Log in" button — primary CTA
5. Error banner — conditional, high-visibility when present

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|                    +------------------------------------+          |
|                    |  [#] Linear App Clone               |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  Email                             |          |
|                    |  [______________________________]  |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  Password                          |          |
|                    |  [______________________________]  |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  [⚠ Invalid email or password]     |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  [====== Log in ==============]    |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    +------------------------------------+          |
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| App logo | (generic `<img>`) | Static branding, no interaction | Alt text for screen readers |
| Email input | TextInput (email variant) | Text entry, validation on blur/ submit | Truncation: show full email via scroll |
| Password input | TextInput (password variant) | Masked entry, optional show/hide toggle | Max length enforced by API |
| Error banner | ErrorBanner | `role="alert"`, appears above submit button on API error | Dismissed when user edits any field |
| Submit button | Button (primary variant) | Submit form, shows spinner in loading state | Disabled during loading, prevented double-click |

## Data Display

Not applicable — this screen has no data tables or lists. Single form with two text inputs.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| App logo heading | "Linear App Clone" | Brand identity, top of card |
| Email label | "Email" | Persistent label above input, not placeholder |
| Email placeholder | "you@example.com" | Hint format, not a label replacement |
| Password label | "Password" | Persistent label above input |
| Password placeholder | (none) | Security best practice — no hint text |
| Submit button | "Log in" | Active voice, concise CTA |
| Error banner | "Invalid email or password" | Generic error — doesn't reveal which field is wrong |
| Network error | "Connection error. Please try again." | Plain language, actionable |

## States

### Populated (Default)

The layout shown in the ASCII sketch above: two filled inputs, no error, enabled button.

### Empty

First-visit state. Both inputs empty, enabled button, no error banner. Same layout as populated but with empty inputs and placeholder text visible.

### Loading

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|                    +------------------------------------+          |
|                    |  [#] Linear App Clone               |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  Email              [disabled]     |          |
|                    |  [__user@mail.com_____________]    |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  Password           [disabled]     |          |
|                    |  [__•_•_•_•_•_•_•_•___________]  |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    |  [=== ⟳ Log in =================] |          |
|                    |                                    |          |
|                    +------------------------------------+          |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

- Email and password inputs are disabled (grayed out, no focus)
- Submit button shows spinner replacing text, disabled
- No error banner visible

### Error

Same layout as Empty/Populated with the ErrorBanner visible above the submit button. Inputs re-enabled for correction. Error text: "Invalid email or password" (generic) or "Connection error. Please try again." (network).

### Success

No visual state — form submission success triggers an immediate redirect to the main app. No success toast or confirmation needed.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Card centered, max-width 480px, comfortable padding |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same as desktop, card margins reduced |
| Mobile (<768px) | Card goes to full-width (margin 16px), stacked layout unchanged |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `main` wrapping the card, `form` with `aria-label="Login"` |
| Heading order | `h1` for app logo heading only |
| Reading / Focus order | Logo → Email input → Password input → Submit button → Error banner (when present) |
| Accessible names | Logo image gets `alt="Linear App Clone"`; show/hide password toggle gets `aria-label` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab between fields in order, Enter submits form, Escape clears error banner |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on all interactive targets |
| Focus not obscured | No sticky regions; inputs visible when focused |
| Non-color intent | Error banner has warning icon + text, not color alone |

## Assumptions

- **Main App screen**: referenced as entry/exit in login and splash flows (e.g., login redirects to "main app", logout returns from it), but not wireframed here. Owned by the system-wireframes document — defines the authenticated app shell (header, sidebar nav, UserAvatar, content area). This auth change assumes that shell exists as the post-login destination.
- **UserAvatar component** (logout dropdown): wired in the design-system, but its containing screen (Main App) is system-wireframes-owned. The component is ready for integration when that shell is built.
- **AuthGuard**: not a standalone screen — a route wrapper component. Correctly excluded from per-screen wireframes. Its runtime behavior is documented in the design-system.
